The full MIT License text is at the end of this file and in
`src/LICENSE_ASTROPAPER`.

This software license does not apply to original writing, original
images, or other content described in the following sections.

2. Blog posts and original hero images
--------------------------------------

Each blog post states its own license in its front matter and on the
published page. That statement is the license for:

- the original textual content of that post; and
- the original hero image created for that post (`header.webp` or the
  image referenced as `ogImage`), when that image is original to this
  site.

Many posts are offered under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-
NoDerivatives 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0):

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/legalcode.en

A later post, translation, or revision may use CC BY-NC-ND 4.0, a
different Creative Commons license, another license, or no public
license at all. Do not assume that every post is CC BY-NC-ND 4.0.
Read the notice on the work you intend to use.

If a post has no license notice, it is not licensed here. See section 4.

3. Third-party material
-----------------------

Screenshots of other software or services, book covers, photographs,
audio, video, embedded third-party pages, and similar material remain
the property of their respective owners. Appearance in a post or in
this repository does not relicense that material, including where the
surrounding post is under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 or another license.

Third-party images are included solely to illustrate the articles, not
for profit. They are used as crestomatía under Mexican law and, where
it applies, as fair use in other jurisdictions.

Videos are embedded from YouTube. Authorship remains with the channels
from which those videos come.

All trademarks mentioned in this repository belong to their respective
owners.

4. Everything else
------------------

Unless a work itself grants a license, all other original material is
copyright Rodolfo González González. All rights reserved. No license is
granted to copy, modify, distribute, or create derivative works of that
material.

This default includes, without limitation:

- pages such as About and Intro, and any other original prose that does
  not carry its own license notice;
- original images that are not a post's original hero image;
- documentation and notes in this repository (for example `AGENTS.md`
  and `PORTAFOLIOS.md`), unless a notice on that file says otherwise.

5. Forking this repository
--------------------------

If you want the Astro Paper theme, fork the upstream repository
instead: https://github.com/satnaing/astro-paper

If you still fork or reuse this repository for the software (MIT), do
not copy original content unless that content's own license allows it.
In particular, remove `src/src/data/blog/` and `src/src/assets/posts/`
unless you have a license to those files, and do not assume that About,
Intro, or other unlicensed pages may be reused.

